#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coth

#% text
# `coth(x)` gives the hyperbolic cotangent 1/tanh(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `coth(x)` stays unevaluated for symbolic `x`; where `tanh(x)` has an exact value, `coth(x)` is its reciprocal.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `coth` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coth(inf)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
coth(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.3130352854993315

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic arguments and symmetry:

#% cell
coth(-x)
#% output
#= -coth(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(coth(1), 30)
#% output
#= 1.313035285499331303636161246930848

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `tanh`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`
